# SARA evaluator API

This file is the evaluator-facing contract. The required scope and output below
are fixed. The factual input contract is also fixed for the Prolog-derived
Catala tests; add internal variables and section subscopes without renaming or
removing these declarations.

- Requirement ID `SARA-TOTAL-TAX`: scope `TotalTax`, output `total_tax`.

> Module Api
> Using Definitions as W
> Using Section1 as S1
> Using Section2 as S2
> Using Section63 as S63
> Using Section68 as S68
> Using Section151 as S151
> Using Section152 as S152
> Using Section3301 as S3301
> Using Section3306 as S3306
> Using Section7703 as S7703

```catala-metadata
declaration scope TotalTax:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input period content W.TaxPeriod
  # Add internal variables and section subscopes here.
  # Keep the predeclared output below unchanged.
  output total_tax content money
```

```catala
# Define TotalTax.total_tax by composing the statutory section scopes. Keep
# cross-section orchestration here rather than assigning it to one provision.
scope TotalTax:
  assertion for all left among (W.all_input_events of world) we have
    for all right among (W.all_input_events of world) we have
      not (W.same_entity of left.identifier, right.identifier and left.kind = right.kind)
      or left = right
  assertion for all left among (W.relationship_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Birth)
    we have for all right among (W.relationship_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Birth)
      we have not (exists person among left.agents such that W.has_agent of right, person)
        or left.starts = [] or right.starts = [] or left.starts = right.starts
  assertion for all income among (W.financial_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Income)
    we have for all payment among (W.financial_events_of_kind of world, W.EventKind.Payment)
      we have not (W.same_entity of income.identifier, payment.identifier)
        or (income.agents = payment.patients
          and income.amounts = payment.amounts
          and income.multiplicity = payment.multiplicity
          and income.starts = payment.starts and income.ends = payment.ends)
```
